**Keydown components** are the Svelte 5 pieces of Keydown: a live editor box, formatted text, a guide with search, tabs, slides, flashcards, charts of math, a style picker and more. This one lite holds all of them in one place, plus `KeydownCore.js` (what they share) and `App.svelte`, a demo page. Press **Start** in the preview and it is compiled right in your browser, so give it a few seconds: `KeydownBox.svelte` carries the whole Keydown engine, every style and every skill inside one file!

It supports everything Keydown can do today:

* the **code block styles** and the **inline code styles**,
* **practice blanks**: `::blank{lines|3|Write here}` and, inside a sentence, `[__8|answer]` and `[##6]`,
* the **dividers**: `::divider{glass|Title|blue}`, the Notched cousins, Gel, Rim and Ticket,
* **page number formats**: `::pagenumbers{roman|1}`,
* drawings (`@@ink`) and the interactive blocks `::chart`, `::poll`, `::quiz`, `::timer` and `::map`,
* live `{{values}}`, custom `@style` tags, and every chip, gel, highlight and unique style.

Use it in your own project by downloading the ZIP and putting the files in one folder, then `import KeydownBox from './KeydownBox.svelte'`. If you are not using Svelte, the same engine comes as one plain `Keydown.js` file on the Radii Office site!


